60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"I lean toward Candidate A. It provides the structural durability I value, avoids the planting failures of the past, and respects the transit patterns Minako observed. It is a pragmatic choice for a depleted staff.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Misaki,,I cannot support Candidate C. Reshaping drainage into ponds would require the deep excavation and heavy earth-moving that the firms warned is risky due to clay subsoil and slippage. It is a recipe for delays.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,"I'm with Benjamin! Candidate A is mostly paved, and since I found out that hard surfaces are way cheaper to maintain than plants, it's the best for the city's wallet! It's super practical!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"I support Candidate A. It requires the least amount of daily manual upkeep, which is essential given our collapsed staffing levels. Unlike B or C, it does not rely on a gardening crew we simply do not have.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minako,,I support Candidate A. It respects the transit patterns of those heading to the tram and avoids the drainage risks associated with the clay subsoil. It is the most realistic option for the site's actual behavior.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It is refreshing to see such a swift consensus. Candidate B would likely mirror the tragedy of the eastern avenue, and Candidate D's facilities would be a maintenance burden we cannot afford. A is the only logical path.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Candidate D is also problematic because it involves significant construction on the southern side, and while that area is easier to hoard, the overall scale of the facilities would still be a risk. A is the safest.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, exactly! And Candidate B would be a total nightmare for the budget with all those trees and gravel paths to look after. Candidate A is just so much easier to keep tidy!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, you are correct. Candidate B would be an operational disaster. Even the volunteer groups we have are already committed to other tasks; we cannot expect them to manage a dense woodland. Candidate A is the only sustainable choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, I agree. Candidate C's ponds would likely fail given the current drainage callouts, and Candidate B ignores the heat readings and transit needs. Candidate A is the only plan that aligns with the physical reality of the park.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,I believe we have exhausted the need for further deliberation. Candidate A is the only option that does not invite a predictable failure. It is a triumph of pragmatism over misplaced ambition.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Candidate A avoids the risks of deep excavation in clay and the logistical nightmare of a total site shutdown. It is the most reliable plan for timely delivery and long-term stability.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,I'm so happy we all agree! Candidate A is definitely the winner. It's the only one that won't leave the city broke or the park a mess in a few years. I'm voting for A!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Asuka,,I also vote for Candidate A. It is the only proposal that acknowledges our staffing crisis and ensures the park remains functional without overextending a depleted workforce. It is the most responsible choice.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minako,,"I vote for Candidate A. It is the only plan that respects the transit flow, the drainage failures, and the staffing constraints. It is the most stable and realistic choice for the park.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I shall cast my vote for Candidate A. It is the only selection that avoids the cycle of grand openings followed by inevitable decay. Logic and history both point to the plaza as the only sustainable path.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Misaki,,"I vote for Candidate A. It is the most realistic option given the ground conditions and the limited availability of firms, ensuring we can actually finish the project without unforeseen delays.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,I'm voting for Candidate A too! It's the only one that makes sense for the budget and the staff. Let's go with the Market Plaza!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over""}]}"
